; ============================================================
; Lite-Writer for the 1802  —  STELLAR text-entry terminal
; (formerly STAR-Writer)
; ============================================================
; Loads at $4000 (VM1 program block).  Relative addressing (default).
;
; Memory layout (dedicated blocks; multitasking suspended via C7 00 at start):
;   $4000..$4336  Program code
;   $4700..$47DE  Status / banner / help strings (rel $0700+)
;   $5000..$57FF  Text buffer (2048 bytes, rel $1000..$17FF)
;   $6000..$67FF  Save bank 1 (2048 bytes, rel $2000..$27FF) — ^S / ^L
;   $6800..$7EFF  reserved for future save banks 2..N
;
; The text buffer and save banks live in the VM2/3/4 RAM ($5000-$7EFF),
; reached via the relative-mode M(Rx) = R[x] + $4000 translation.  Lite-Writer
; issues C7 00 (SETMULTI off) right after CD so the scheduler stays on VM1 and
; those blocks are ours alone.  (Hardware-validated: rel $1000/$2000 r/w OK.)
;
; Control keys:
;   CR        store CR+LF, echo CR+LF
;   BS        backspace - drop last char (drops 2 on a CR+LF pair),
;             echo BS SP BS.  Accepts BOTH $08 (Ctrl-H) and $7F (DEL),
;             so the Mac/VT Backspace key works whichever byte it sends.
;   ^D ($04)  delete one char (drops 2 on a CR+LF pair)
;   ^K ($0B)  kill line.  If the current line has text: erase it back to the
;             previous CR+LF (in-place BS SP BS feedback), keep that CR+LF,
;             write a $00 EOF marker (Path A).  If the current line is EMPTY
;             (just pressed Enter): roll back THROUGH the previous CR+LF and
;             kill the previous line too, write $00, then redraw via the ^V
;             view (Path B).  Repeated ^K walks backward one line per press;
;             stops cleanly at the buffer start.
;   ^E ($05)  end - jump to end of saved text, replay it, keep typing
;   ^U ($15)  clear - zero the whole buffer, reset pointer
;   ^V ($16)  view buffer
;   ^S ($13)  SAVE text into save bank 1 at $6000 ("File Saved")
;   ^L ($0C)  LOAD save bank 1 ($6000) back into the text buffer + display
;   ^W ($17)  WRITE text to a chosen location.  Prompts "Where? ", reads 4
;             hex digits = a full 16-bit rel address, copies the text buffer
;             there, replies "Copied".  E.g. 2000 -> rel $2000 -> real $6000
;             (save bank 1); 1000 -> $5000 (the buffer).  d1 d2 = HIGH byte,
;             d3 d4 = LOW byte.
;   ^G ($07)  help screen
;   ^X ($18)  exit - write $00 sentinel at M(R1), HALT (text remains)
;
; KEY-CODE NOTES (terminals disagree on these — chosen to avoid clashes):
;   * Backspace: many terminals (incl. macOS Terminal) send $7F (DEL) for
;     the Backspace key, others send $08 (Ctrl-H).  Backspace therefore
;     handles BOTH codes.  Help is NOT on ^? ($7F) — $7F is the Backspace.
;   * Help: moved from ^? ($7F) to ^G ($07), which every terminal can type.
;   * Write: on ^W (not ^M) because Ctrl-M == $0D == Enter, the newline key.
;
; OPCODE NOTE: this build's CLEARA ($6A) handler is buggy (it crashed the VM
;   — CORE showed last command $6A).  The ^W handler therefore zeroes the
;   Accumulator with LOADAI 00 00 ($10 00 00) instead of CLEARA.
;
; ^W detail: 4 hex digits form a full 16-bit rel offset (d1 d2 d3 d4).
;   d1,d2 -> HIGH byte of the dest pointer; d3,d4 -> LOW byte.  Each byte is
;   built from two nibbles (nibble<<4 + nibble), so no 16-bit shift is
;   needed — only a SWAPA to promote the HIGH byte.  In relative mode the VM
;   adds $4000, so rel $0000-$3EFF reaches real $4000-$7EFF.  Valid hex chars
;   are 0-9 and A-F (uppercase).  Example: 2000 -> rel $2000 -> real $6000.
;
; Status strings:
;   "Lite-Writer for the 1802" + CRLF   — banner at start-up
;   "Text is Present"                   — at start-up if M($5000)!=0
;   "You are nearing the size limit"    — once, when R1 reaches $17E0
;   "File Saved"                        — after ^S copies text to $6000
;   "Where? "                           — ^W prompt for the destination
;   "Copied"                            — after ^W copies the text
;
; vCPU register map:
;   R1 = write pointer        R2 = buffer start  ($1000)
;   R3 = buffer end+1 ($1800) R4 = scratch iterator
;   R5 = buffer last ($17FF)  R6/R7 = copy src/dst (save/load/^W, peek)
;   R9 = warn threshold ($17E0)   RA = string pointer (print loops)
;   R8 = hex-compare constant ($000A)   RB = scratch (^W hex-digit decode)
;
; Custom terminal I/O opcodes used by this build (not in the base set):
;   INCH  $CB        wait for a keystroke -> Acc low byte
;   OUTCH $C9        output Acc low byte to the terminal as ASCII
;   OUTL  $CA NN     output literal byte NN to the terminal as ASCII
;
; Assembled + label-checked (every GTL/IFTRUEL/IFFALSEL target verified to
; have a matching LBL; stream decodes cleanly $4000..$4336 with no stray
; bytes; 51 labels, 81 targets matched).  C7 00 = SETMULTI off (see firmware).
; ============================================================

; ---- FULL DISASSEMBLY ----
